From: GPU lane (diagnosis 2026-11-21); rebased onto the tree CI actually compiles, by baseband lane
Subject: 0504 sweet_ufs pl_thread: make pandora_reboot_after independent of the log file

The bounded reset used to be checked at the bottom of pl_thread's loop, after pl_flush(), and one
failed UFS write returned from the logging thread entirely -- silently cancelling the reset for the
rest of the boot.  pl_flush() -> ufs_write_blocks() -> ufs_scsi() is a blocking disk write that can
return ETIMEDOUT, so a single transient failure left the phone in iOS with USB enumerated until
somebody reset it by hand.  On 2026-11-21 that happened: a 30-minute trial started at 08:51 and the
phone did not come back for eight hours, blocking every other lane waiting for the device.

The fix: check the deadline FIRST, before taking the UFS lock or touching the disk, and on a write
failure only clear pl_ready instead of returning, so the thread keeps waking up and the deadline
keeps firing.  The orderly-shutdown branch is preserved verbatim.

Why this rebase (and why the previous two versions never worked): the first 0504 and its CarPlay
rebase were written against pl_psci_reset()/a pre-0481 body; `git apply` failed at
bsd/dev/sweet_ufs.c:2219/2224 and CI logged "Skipping patch ... (already upstream, previously
applied, or malformed)".  They were never in a single kernel.  The current tree ends the deadline
branch with reboot_kernel(RB_AUTOBOOT, NULL) ("shutting down cleanly"), so this diff is generated
against that exact file, taken from the xnu-buildtree artifact of CI run 44863365869.

diff --git a/bsd/dev/sweet_ufs.c b/b/bsd/dev/sweet_ufs.c
index e99cb27..b875684 100755
--- a/bsd/dev/sweet_ufs.c
+++ b/bsd/dev/sweet_ufs.c
@@ -2223,6 +2223,38 @@ pl_thread(__unused void *arg, __unused wait_result_t wr)
 	nanoseconds_to_absolutetime((uint64_t)iostats * NSEC_PER_SEC, &io_every);
 	for (;;) {
 		(void)tsleep(&pl_chan, PZERO, "pandoralog", hz * (int)secs);
+		/*
+		 * 0504: the bounded reset must not be hostage to the log file.
+		 *
+		 * The deadline used to be checked at the bottom of this loop, after pl_flush(), and
+		 * one failed write returned from this thread entirely.  pl_flush() ->
+		 * ufs_write_blocks() -> ufs_scsi() is a blocking disk write that can return
+		 * ETIMEDOUT, so a single transient failure silently cancelled pandora_reboot_after
+		 * for the rest of the boot: the phone stayed in iOS with USB enumerated until
+		 * somebody reset it by hand (2026-11-21, eight hours, every other lane blocked).
+		 *
+		 * So the deadline is checked first, before anything touches the disk, and a write
+		 * failure only stops the logging -- never the reset.
+		 */
+		if (limit && mach_absolute_time() - start >= limit) {
+			printf("PANDORA: pandora_reboot_after=%u reached, shutting down cleanly\n", reboot_after);
+			/* A bounded trial is a normal shutdown, not a panic. Non-journaled HFS
+			 * bitmap buffers use delayed writes: resetting here can persist catalog
+			 * extents without their allocation bits and let the next boot reuse live data.
+			 * Use the existing process-stop/sync/unmount/buffer-drain path without the
+			 * UFS lock held. Its final PE_halt_restart still drains the console and resets.
+			 * Never fall back to an unsynced reset if another shutdown owns the system. */
+			int shutdown_error = reboot_kernel(RB_AUTOBOOT, NULL);
+			printf("PANDORA: orderly timed shutdown returned %d; no forced reset\n", shutdown_error);
+			limit = 0; /* do not repeat a shutdown request; retain console evidence */
+		}
+		/*
+		 * Logging has stopped (a write failed once): keep waking up so the deadline above
+		 * keeps firing, but stay off the disk entirely from here on.
+		 */
+		if (!pl_ready) {
+			continue;
+		}
 		lck_mtx_lock(&sweet_ufs_lock);
 		uint64_t now = mach_absolute_time();
 		if (io_every && now - io_last >= io_every) {
@@ -2240,19 +2272,6 @@ pl_thread(__unused void *arg, __unused wait_result_t wr)
 		if (error) {
 			printf("PANDORA LOG: write failed (%d), log stopped\n", error);
 			pl_ready = false;
-			return;
-		}
-		if (limit && mach_absolute_time() - start >= limit) {
-			printf("PANDORA: pandora_reboot_after=%u reached, shutting down cleanly\n", reboot_after);
-			/* A bounded trial is a normal shutdown, not a panic. Non-journaled HFS
-			 * bitmap buffers use delayed writes: resetting here can persist catalog
-			 * extents without their allocation bits and let the next boot reuse live data.
-			 * Use the existing process-stop/sync/unmount/buffer-drain path without the
-			 * UFS lock held. Its final PE_halt_restart still drains the console and resets.
-			 * Never fall back to an unsynced reset if another shutdown owns the system. */
-			int shutdown_error = reboot_kernel(RB_AUTOBOOT, NULL);
-			printf("PANDORA: orderly timed shutdown returned %d; no forced reset\n", shutdown_error);
-			limit = 0; /* do not repeat a shutdown request; retain console evidence */
 		}
 	}
 }
